.Dd October 25, 2026
.Dt SU 1
.Os Werewolf
.Sh NAME
.Nm su
.Nd authenticate a new root login through the forwarded SSH agent
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl
.Op Cm root
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The Werewolf
.Nm
utility opens a fresh root SSH login to 127.0.0.1:22.
All accepted invocations open the same root login shell.
It has no set-user-ID privilege; the existing SSH server authenticates
the key and creates the session.
.Pp
The caller must be in an interactive SSH session with terminal input and
output and a forwarded agent.
The wrapper uses only its system SSH configuration and host-key pin.
It disables connection sharing, further forwarding, local identity files,
password prompts and SSH escape commands.
Missing or mismatched host pins fail without a trust prompt.
.Pp
Only PATH, TERM and SSH_AUTH_SOCK are passed to the client.
Other target accounts, arbitrary commands and gained privileges are refused.
Authentication follows the image's sshd policy; playground permits
ordinary keys as well as security keys.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width SSH_AUTH_SOCK
.It Ev SSH_AUTH_SOCK
Forwarded agent socket containing a key authorized for root.
.It Ev SSH_CONNECTION , SSH_TTY
Interactive-session hints, checked for diagnostics but not used as credentials.
.It Ev TERM
Terminal type passed to the SSH client.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/ssh/su_config
Fixed client configuration.
.It Pa /run/werewolf/ssh_known_hosts
Local host-key pin published before sshd starts.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
After successful execution of the SSH client, its exit status is returned.
Setup or validation failure produces a nonzero status.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssh-host-key 8
.Sh CAVEATS
A compromised operator session can request agent signatures or interfere
with the terminal.
A fresh root SSH connection from the operator's own machine avoids passing
the root terminal through that session.
